  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Methyl orange is a popular pH indicator that is used in the acid base&nbsp;titration.Unlike a universal indicator, methyl orange does not have a full spectrum of color change, but it has a sharp end point.The colour of the solution changes from yellow to&nbsp;red when methyl orange is used as an indicator.That means in acidic medium it is red and exists in&nbsp;quinonoid form<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/19ab576e-db34-47e3-b373-e5386a6d8d5f-8-8-2022new.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 200px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
